{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1191171-how-defined-can-you-make-nova-powers","id":1191171,"title":"How defined can you make Nova powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T17:18:29-08:00","id":1191171,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon11.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How defined can you make Nova powers?","content":"So I never had a copy of Aberrant but it intrigued me. How defined can you make Nova powers? Do they have to be broad? Like can I make a Nova that can control only fear instead of all emotions? Can I make a Nova that can say only sprout claws or turn into a wolf rather then shapeshift? Can I have someone that only controls say wood or water?<br /> <br /> And are Stalwarts just low powered stable Novas essentially?<br /> <br /> And what about super powered beings that aren\u2019t harnessing quantum or Psi? Like strongmen and really smart people that aren\u2019t Novas, maybe just science/evolution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T01:35:51-08:00","id":1191285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1191171-how-defined-can-you-make-nova-powers#post1191171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I never had a copy of Aberrant but it intrigued me. How defined can you make Nova powers? Do they have to be broad? Like can I make a Nova that can control only fear instead of all emotions? Can I make a Nova that can say only sprout claws or turn into a wolf rather then shapeshift? Can I have someone that only controls say wood or water?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the individual power (also, in case it needs to be said, I'm talking about 1e rules here). Some of them are pretty specific -- Quantum Bolt is an energy blast, and you get to decide just what sort of energy, and each dot makes that blast better. But then you get powers like Weather Manipulation, where each dot lets you select a different ability. The Aberrant Player's Guide, however, does have some pretty detailed customization rules, letting you do things like 'control a single emotion' or 'have a limited range of forms.' It varies based on individual powers (and the higher level the power the more broad it is), but there is a lot of room to define specific abilities -- especially if you have the Player's Guide and have a flexible Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1191171-how-defined-can-you-make-nova-powers#post1191171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are Stalwarts just low powered stable Novas essentially?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer, yes. Stalwarts' (and Mesmerists') upper-level Knacks are about on par with what Novas can casually start with if they see fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1191171-how-defined-can-you-make-nova-powers#post1191171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what about super powered beings that aren\u2019t harnessing quantum or Psi? Like strongmen and really smart people that aren\u2019t Novas, maybe just science/evolution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant never really touched on that at all (unless you count people using steroids and similar drugs derived from Nova physiology). Adventure! does, somewhat, but even then there's usually some sort of Inspired science behind anyone with superhuman abilities -- they've been directly modified by a mad scientist, or some z-wave artifact or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:24:31-08:00","id":1191364,"title":"","content":"I feel like if you want Doc Savage-style &quot;maximum human potential&quot; characters that aren't overtly super-powered, you're looking at Talents. Perhaps Talents with lots of XP spent on Gifts, for the upper range characters like Batman or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T12:16:10-08:00","id":1191709,"title":"","content":"The Aberrant players Guide had rules for adding limitations to powers to lower their costs/power rank.<br /> <br /> I don't know where my copy is ATM, but as best memory serves, you could do things like get a discount because Growth was on permanently and you had to spend quantum to be normal sized. Or Growth was able to be like a Level 1 power instead of Level 2 if you had 1 alternate size instead of having control. So like normal Growth you can go from 6 foot to 7 foot, 12 foot, 20 foot, whatever you need and are able to roll/pay for. Limited growth you are either your normal size or say 15 foot no in-between, no taller.<br /> <br /> Density shift for only one direction (just turn harder OR just turn into a ghost, not both)<br /> <br /> Shapeshift into one specific form was another example, I think it dropped shapeshift by a category level.<br /> <br /> Other things involved linking powers. I forget all the things now.<br /> <br /> But the point is there were rules, but they were in a supplemental book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}